Falsifies `system_tests::user::syscall_fuzzer_tests::seeded_syscalls_agree_with_the_shadow_model`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64 (the hunk is portable scheduler code).

The defect is the one `revocation_in_flight_tests` records, applied unchanged: the revocation sweep
for `PageFrame` stops reading `Thread::outgoing_cap`, so a frame staged in a parked `SEND_CAPABILITY`
survives `PageFrame::REVOKE` and the next `RECEIVE_CAPABILITY` files it in the receiver's table. It is one
of the six defects milestone 752 (a seeded syscall driver with a shadow model) was measured
against; the other five are in that block's table, with the seed and call each turned red.

Expected to fail: seed 559 (corpus), step 14, `RECEIVE_CAPABILITY` returns `x1 = 5` (the revoked frame's
new slot) where the shadow model says `NO_CAP`, reported as `syscall fuzzer: seed 0x22f step 14:
actor 0 Invoke { slot: 1, method: 3, a: [0, 0, 0] } answered ... regs: [5, 0, 9, 0] ... (replay:
NIFE_SYSCALL_FUZZ_SEEDS=559:1)`. History: red on aarch64 2026-10-04 (UTC) by the lane for milestone
752 at seed 5, step 39; after §246 (a plain `RECEIVE` never takes a capability), a PROVISIONAL
number, diverged the walk, PR #1611 swept 2,000 seeds under this patch, found seed 342, added it to
the corpus, and replayed it red on aarch64.

Regenerated 2026-10-04 (UTC) by the lane for the proposal "capability lookup off the global lock",
which moved each thread's capability table out of `Thread` and behind its own lock: the sweep now
iterates `(thread, table)` pairs, so the old hunk no longer matched. Same removal, same defect; the
added `let _ = t;` only keeps the patched build free of an unused-variable warning.
Replayed red on aarch64 the same day: seed 5, step 39, `regs: [5, ...]` against the model's `NO_CAP`.

Re-found 2026-10-08 (UTC) by milestone 139 (drive the unsafe count down) round 10's lane, the
scheduler queue ownership token: the walk diverged again on main before that lane's cut
(2026-10-07), and seed 342 stayed green with
this defect applied, verified by hand at the lane's claim commit `2d55858b2` (the token work is not
its cause). A 5,000-seed sweep under this patch on aarch64 found it red first at seed 559, step 14;
dead 342 left the corpus for 559. The full `script/falsifications --sweep system_tests` replayed it
red on aarch64, riscv64 and x86_64 the same day.

Regenerated 2026-10-11 (UTC) for milestone 840 (the scheduler file is split along its seams):
the same lines, moved out of `kernel/src/sched.rs` into `kernel/src/sched/capabilities.rs` unchanged, so the defect is
the same and only the path and line numbers differ.

